  symptoms: {
    hero1: [
      { symptom: 'Dead display, no banner at power-up', suspects: ['cpu6808'], note: 'Check the charger first (13.9 V float, 5.6 V reference at TP8/TP9). Then the logic +5 V and motor +12 V supplies, then the display board (P1201 pin 8 high). TM printed p. 54-55.' },
      { symptom: 'Robot awake, no speech', suspects: ['sc01a'], note: 'Speech power is $C2E0 bit 3 through P501 pin 11. Check STB (P501 pin 3 to SC-01A pin 7) and A/R (P501 pin 4 to pin 8). TM printed p. 78-79.' },
      { symptom: 'Speech stops after one sound, or speech runs too fast or slow', suspects: ['sc01a'], note: 'A/R stuck low stops speech after one phoneme. R15 sets the clock: reference pitch and speed (TM printed p. 79).' },
      { symptom: 'Drive too slow, or will not start at low speed', suspects: [], note: 'Wrong ROM for the drive board. Versions 1.0 and 1.U suit the potentiometer board; 1.1 and 1.3 suit the later board. Low and medium drive values differ (ROM FAQ, table at $E32B).' },
      { symptom: 'RAM lost after sleep, or program corrupt after sleep', suspects: ['sram6116'], note: 'RAM stays on the retained VSB rail (U326) while main logic sleeps about 10 s. U322 blocks writes for about 100 ms after wake. Check U321 timing (R317/C324) and Q301 (power spec notes).' },
      { symptom: 'Robot dead for about 10 s after a sleep command, then wakes', suspects: [], note: 'Normal: the sleep one-shot removes the main +5 V logic rail for about 10 s. If it never returns, check U321 and Q301.' },
      { symptom: 'Serial terminal wrong baud rate or garbled', suspects: ['cpu6808'], note: 'Serial timing is in the ROM loops. The 4 MHz ROMs (1.U, 1.3) need the ET-18-6 or a 4 MHz crystal. A ROM that does not match the clock changes the baud rate.' },
      { symptom: 'Sonar reading stuck at one value, or no reading', suspects: ['adc0804'], note: 'A constant $FF means the sense rail is missing. Check the sonar power and TP1/TP2 on the sense board (TM sonar check).' }
    ],
    herojr: [
      { symptom: 'Green POWER LED off after ON and RESET', suspects: ['pia6821'], note: 'Owner guide: rear POWER off, dead battery or blown fuse. TM chart (printed p. 13-14): battery wiring, low battery, fuse F1, keyboard and reset circuit, TP201 jumper.' },
      { symptom: 'Robot does not speak; red data LEDs flash', suspects: [], note: 'TM chart: check battery wiring, low battery, fuse F1, keyboard, the U302, Q301, Q302, U221 and U222 circuits, and the TP201 jumper.' },
      { symptom: 'Speech distorted while red LEDs flash', suspects: ['sc01a'], note: 'TM chart: R224 misadjusted; D202, Q202, Q203; then U201, U215 and U223. Check R224 first.' },
      { symptom: 'Drive wheel does not turn, or turns only in reverse', suspects: ['cpu6808', 'pia6821'], note: 'TM chart: U201 or U214 for no turn; U214 or U215 for reverse only. Check the motor driver (Q321) and its PIA lines.' },
      { symptom: 'Sonar malfunction: no sound from transducer', suspects: ['pia6821'], note: 'TM chart: check the transducer A4 lead to P305, then U214 or U215. Sonar INIT is U214 pin 19 (CB2); echo is U215 pin 18 (CB1).' },
      { symptom: 'Malfunction in memory circuits', suspects: ['sram6116', 'rom27128'], note: 'TM chart lists U203-U208. Check the RAM and ROM sockets and their jumper plugs (J201-J210) first.' },
      { symptom: 'No keyboard keys respond', suspects: ['pia6821'], note: 'TM chart: check plugs P204 and P205, then U214. The RESET key is on the reset circuit, not the keypad.' },
      { symptom: 'Robot sleeps and does not wake; green LED blinks only every 5 s', suspects: ['rtc146818'], note: 'The every-5 s flash is the normal sleep catnap. If it stays asleep, check the SLEEP-NORM switch (SW2), any pending alarm (RESET cancels it), and the RTC wake path.' }
    ]
  },

